# mtkclient fix: Disable "Reconnect to stage2 with higher speed"
#
# On Windows 11 with UsbDk, the baud-rate change and port reopen after
# DA stage-2 upload consistently fails (exit code 5). The actual flash
# works fine at the default (full) USB speed, so we hard-disable the
# reconnect block.
#
# File: mtkclient/Library/DA/legacy/dalegacy_lib.py, line 654
#
# Apply:
#   Change:
#     if speed[0] == 0 and self.daconfig.reconnect:
#   To:
#     if False and speed[0] == 0 and self.daconfig.reconnect:  # FORCED OFF
#
# After this patch, a BROM-mode flash runs to completion:
#   Preloader -> Kamakiri -> DA stage-1 -> DA stage-2 (upload)
#   -> [SKIP reconnect] -> Write partition -> exit 0
#
# Confirmed working on:
#   Device: Alcatel 8082 (TCL U3A_10_WIFI, MT6580), Android 8.1
#   Host:   Windows 11 Pro build 26200, mtkclient 2.1.4, UsbDk
